## Q7. Write the complete HTML code for the personal introduction webpage.

**Answer:**

Create a file named `index.html` and copy the following code into it.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Personal Introduction</title>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- Header Section -->
    <header>
        <h1>Naman Pratap</h1>
        <p>B.Tech Computer Science Student</p>
    </header>

    <hr>

    <!-- About Me Section -->
    <section>
        <h2>About Me</h2>
        <p>
            My name is Naman Pratap. I am a first-year B.Tech
            Computer Science student. I am learning web development
            and programming to improve my technical skills.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <!-- Education Section -->
    <section>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <h3>Bachelor of Technology</h3>
        <p>Stream: Computer Science</p>
        <p>Currently pursuing my first year of B.Tech.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <!-- Technical Skills Section -->
    <section>
        <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>HTML</li>
            <li>CSS</li>
            <li>Java</li>
            <li>Basic Programming</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <!-- Hobbies Section -->
    <section>
        <h2>Hobbies</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Learning new technologies</li>
            <li>Practicing coding</li>
            <li>Playing sports</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <!-- Contact Information Section -->
    <section>
        <h2>Contact Information</h2>
        <p>Email: student@example.com</p>
        <p>Contact: Available on request</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer Section -->
    <footer>
        <p>Thank you for visiting my webpage!</p>
    </footer>

</body>

</html>
```

## Q8. How do you save and run the HTML file?

**Answer:**

1. Open Visual Studio Code.
2. Create a file named `index.html`.
3. Paste the complete HTML code into the file.
4. Press `Ctrl + S` to save the file.
5. Right-click inside the editor.
6. Select **Open with Live Server**.
7. Check that all sections appear correctly in the browser.

## Q9. How do you commit the final code to a Git repository?

**Answer:**

Open the terminal inside your project folder and run:

```bash
git status
git add index.html
git commit -m "Complete HTML foundations mini-project"
```

If the project has already been connected to GitHub, upload the commit using:

```bash
git push
```

If the repository has not been connected to GitHub, create a GitHub repository and configure the remote before running `git push`.

